00:08:29,268 --> 00:08:34,012
[SPEAKER_08]: My police officers have seen some things that are really tragic and have been

90
00:08:35,121 --> 00:08:35,902
[SPEAKER_08]: quite impactful.

91
00:08:36,062 --> 00:08:39,885
[SPEAKER_08]: I have a very young police department, and regardless of that, it impacts young and old.

92
00:08:40,305 --> 00:08:43,507
[SPEAKER_08]: So we've spent significant time on the health and wellness of our police officers.

93
00:08:44,528 --> 00:08:48,411
[SPEAKER_08]: We've done required suicide prevention police officers.

94
00:08:48,511 --> 00:08:50,933
[SPEAKER_08]: It's the number one killer for police officers in the country.

95
00:08:51,333 --> 00:09:03,642
[SPEAKER_08]: But we're finding very, very much success in training police officers, both within our department and reaching out to the greater Boston crisis intervention and support teams to bring them in and have conversations with our police officers, kind of

