1156
01:30:14,278 --> 01:30:14,618
[SPEAKER_12]: Thank you.

1157
01:30:15,078 --> 01:30:15,558
[SPEAKER_03]: Good evening.

1158
01:30:16,940 --> 01:30:23,323
[SPEAKER_03]: First, I'd like to humbly thank the administration for allowing me to present this.

1159
01:30:25,044 --> 01:30:34,329
[SPEAKER_03]: This budget was created back in April with help from one of the people in finance, the assistant director at the time.

1160
01:30:35,670 --> 01:30:42,033
[SPEAKER_03]: And it had some changes and Nina and I have discussed those changes.

1161
01:30:42,253 --> 01:30:45,375
[SPEAKER_03]: I mean, the chief of staff and I have discussed those changes.

1162
01:30:46,284 --> 01:30:58,530
[SPEAKER_03]: So I would like just to read our small overview of our department.

1163
01:30:59,191 --> 01:31:06,354
[SPEAKER_03]: The registrar voters election office conducts elections and maintains vital voter registration data for the city of Medford.

1164
01:31:07,475 --> 01:31:10,617
[SPEAKER_03]: Essentially we work for the residents of the city of Medford.

1165
01:31:11,437 --> 01:31:14,859
[SPEAKER_03]: The office tracks and maintains voter registration data

1166
01:31:16,052 --> 01:31:30,595
[SPEAKER_03]: Office staff registers new voters, documents applications for absentee and mail-in ballots, processes the ballots cast for early voting, maintains and securely stores blank and processed ballots for all elections.

1167
01:31:31,456 --> 01:31:36,257
[SPEAKER_03]: We follow and adhere to all city, state, and federal voting laws.

1168
01:31:37,137 --> 01:31:41,478
[SPEAKER_03]: Each full-time person is trained in the operation and use of the Poll Pat system.

1169
01:31:42,378 --> 01:32:03,402
[SPEAKER_03]: The poll pad system for those of you who don't know allows us to create our own database for voting elections, meaning that rather than sending it out to a vendor, the vendors come and will train us on how to do it so it can be uploaded to the poll pad and reduce the amount of paper.

1170
01:32:04,482 --> 01:32:10,143
[SPEAKER_03]: That was very important to us is that we get sort of in the 21st century and go a little more green.

1171
01:32:12,638 --> 01:32:20,440
[SPEAKER_03]: We also are trained in the Office of Campaign Finance, State Ethics Commission, and record retention.

1172
01:32:21,420 --> 01:32:26,362
[SPEAKER_03]: We maintain a current list of eligible voters, as well as all residents for the city of Medford.

1173
01:32:27,902 --> 01:32:31,283
[SPEAKER_03]: On March 29th, we separated from the city clerk's office.

1174
01:32:32,323 --> 01:32:39,085
[SPEAKER_03]: In that time, we have confirmed three election commissioners by collaboration with the mayor's office and the city council.

1175
01:32:40,127 --> 01:32:50,773
[SPEAKER_03]: We've scheduled community-wide voter registration, and we are participating currently in the anonymous voting program sponsored by Secretary Galvin's office.

1176
01:32:52,094 --> 01:33:04,021
[SPEAKER_03]: We created and implemented a supervised voting program for nursing homes, for those facilities, so their votes are protected, and we know that the votes are accurate.

1177
01:33:05,141 --> 01:33:07,523
[SPEAKER_03]: Through ARPA money and support of the mayor,

1178
01:33:08,427 --> 01:33:09,948
[SPEAKER_03]: We have purchased new voting booths.

1179
01:33:10,288 --> 01:33:14,251
[SPEAKER_03]: There's one in that corner and there's one to my right behind me.

1180
01:33:15,271 --> 01:33:20,115
[SPEAKER_03]: This is the first time in 39 years, the city has purchased new voting equipment.

1181
01:33:21,175 --> 01:33:28,780
[SPEAKER_03]: Additionally, with the support of the mayor and through ARPA money, we purchased poll pads to take Medford into the 21st century.

1182
01:33:30,820 --> 01:33:31,380
[SPEAKER_03]: with voting.

1183
01:33:31,940 --> 01:33:41,124
[SPEAKER_03]: We make a pledge to reduce paper as much as possible, and we're implementing a community-wide education service and series.

1184
01:33:42,524 --> 01:33:45,685
[SPEAKER_03]: We've done the series once in May.

1185
01:33:46,665 --> 01:33:48,186
[SPEAKER_03]: It was extremely popular.

1186
01:33:50,787 --> 01:33:56,949
[SPEAKER_03]: With the help of the Medford Cable TV, we're going to run the same series

1187
01:33:57,671 --> 01:33:59,813
[SPEAKER_03]: that were recorded in October again.

1188
01:34:00,313 --> 01:34:06,939
[SPEAKER_03]: I think it's very important that the voters of Medford understand the terminology and how things are progressing.

1189
01:34:09,801 --> 01:34:15,586
[SPEAKER_03]: Some of the upcoming critical issues that we have is cybersecurity.

1190
01:34:17,047 --> 01:34:25,695
[SPEAKER_03]: In the last 24 hours, we have received three requests for two online trainings for cybersecurity

1191
01:34:26,658 --> 01:34:32,280
[SPEAKER_03]: as well as an in-person training that's being offered by Secretary Galvin's office.

1192
01:34:33,280 --> 01:34:41,744
[SPEAKER_03]: The reason that cybersecurity is so important for this election season, this is what is considered the federal midterm election.

1193
01:34:43,144 --> 01:34:53,688
[SPEAKER_03]: And they are thinking, higher up thinking cybersecurity people, that actors

1194
01:34:55,245 --> 01:35:09,430
[SPEAKER_03]: will begin dry runs of how to infiltrate every election system, be it by application or whatever, showing up and saying I'm so-and-so and I'm registered to vote.

1195
01:35:10,570 --> 01:35:19,633
[SPEAKER_03]: So there's a lot of training that's going to have to go around for not just office staff, commissioners, but for poll workers too.

1196
01:35:20,494 --> 01:35:25,636
[SPEAKER_03]: The other piece of that is poll workers are going to have to be trained.

1197
01:35:26,176 --> 01:35:35,279
[SPEAKER_03]: And this is still in conversations and talks about different scenarios and how to diffuse them on election day.

1198
01:35:38,482 --> 01:35:42,505
[SPEAKER_03]: the dry run would be for the 2024 presidential election.

1199
01:35:43,466 --> 01:35:46,188
[SPEAKER_03]: So those are the things that we're working on.

1200
01:35:46,948 --> 01:35:55,475
[SPEAKER_03]: It would be our goal to continue with the community-wide voter education series, as well as collaborative projects with the Medford High School.

1201
01:35:56,836 --> 01:36:04,942
[SPEAKER_03]: One of the commissioners and myself did a registration up there in June, and

1202
01:36:07,263 --> 01:36:19,213
[SPEAKER_03]: it was amazing to me how many young people are going off to college in the fall and didn't realize that they could still vote in their own city or town.

1203
01:36:20,574 --> 01:36:34,166
[SPEAKER_03]: So in conversations with staff at the high school, it was brought to my attention that perhaps I could go there in October and educate these young people

1204
01:36:34,938 --> 01:36:43,540
[SPEAKER_03]: on the importance of voting, why it's important that you vote in your hometown, because you're gonna go to college and then you're gonna come back and you're still gonna be a resident here.

1205
01:36:45,621 --> 01:36:54,263
[SPEAKER_03]: We continue to offer professional five-star customer service, so each voter and resident knows their value and importance.

1206
01:36:55,083 --> 01:37:01,265
[SPEAKER_03]: Their voice, which is their vote, is very, very important to us.

1207
01:37:02,871 --> 01:37:14,599
[SPEAKER_03]: We work collaboratively with other departments, DPW, the police department, and community development to increase the response to our annual street listing and city census.

1208
01:37:15,499 --> 01:37:19,502
[SPEAKER_03]: And I'd be happy to take any questions that you may have on the budget.

1209
01:37:20,282 --> 01:37:20,903
[SPEAKER_12]: Thank you.

1210
01:37:21,823 --> 01:37:22,984
[SPEAKER_12]: Questions from the council.

1211
01:37:25,506 --> 01:37:27,387
[SPEAKER_12]: I have a few, oh, Councilor Collins.

1212
01:37:29,027 --> 01:37:34,450
[SPEAKER_01]: Thank you, Vice President Behrs, and thank you so much, Sandy, for being here today and taking us through your budget.

1213
01:37:37,131 --> 01:37:39,752
[SPEAKER_01]: This all, you know, is very comprehensive.

1214
01:37:39,812 --> 01:37:41,172
[SPEAKER_01]: My question is more of a general one.

1215
01:37:42,433 --> 01:37:48,036
[SPEAKER_01]: I know that, you know, across all of City Hall, you know, the belt is being tightened this year by necessity.

1216
01:37:48,636 --> 01:37:51,037
[SPEAKER_01]: I see that your department is overall taking about a

1217
01:37:52,312 --> 01:37:54,853
[SPEAKER_01]: 13.5% deduction from last year.

1218
01:37:54,873 --> 01:37:59,376
[SPEAKER_01]: I know that a lot of thought went into those strategic reductions.

1219
01:38:00,436 --> 01:38:06,899
[SPEAKER_01]: I also know that the profile of an office such as yours is only getting more important as time goes on.

1220
01:38:06,939 --> 01:38:09,280
[SPEAKER_01]: Just earlier today, I was listening to the news about the midterms.

1221
01:38:09,881 --> 01:38:20,906
[SPEAKER_01]: I think that as with a lot of issues, we would be remiss to think that election security, streamlining of elections, modernizing, professionalizing of elections is something that Medford doesn't have to be.

1222
01:38:21,526 --> 01:38:22,167
[SPEAKER_01]: concerned about.

1223
01:38:22,187 --> 01:38:28,530
[SPEAKER_01]: So I'm really glad to see the focus so far that's been put on this office in our city.

1224
01:38:28,550 --> 01:38:38,876
[SPEAKER_01]: And I guess I'm curious overall, what your through this budget, you know, do you feel empowered to do the work that you think needs to be done by this fall for going forward?

1225
01:38:38,916 --> 01:38:44,120
[SPEAKER_01]: And what would be what would be the key priorities in your mind for making sure that we're ready for 2024?

1226
01:38:45,403 --> 01:38:48,384
[SPEAKER_03]: Thank you, Councillor Collins for that question.

1227
01:38:48,705 --> 01:38:56,509
[SPEAKER_03]: I did have an opportunity to speak with Chief of Staff Nazarian prior to this meeting.

1228
01:38:57,249 --> 01:39:07,274
[SPEAKER_03]: And one of the line items that concerned me, actually there were two, is the salaries part-time.

1229
01:39:08,507 --> 01:39:16,331
[SPEAKER_03]: And initially when the budget was done back in April, I believe it was bumped to 65,000.

1230
01:39:17,771 --> 01:39:26,195
[SPEAKER_03]: Now what comes out of that salaries part-time is everybody and everything elections.

1231
01:39:27,116 --> 01:39:32,538
[SPEAKER_03]: So in the city right now, well, as of last year, it costs us about $26,000.

1232
01:39:32,618 --> 01:39:33,618
[SPEAKER_03]: That is early voting,

1233
01:39:38,539 --> 01:39:45,561
[SPEAKER_03]: the mail-out voting, the in-person voting at the polling locations.

1234
01:39:46,041 --> 01:39:51,782
[SPEAKER_03]: So I did speak with Chief of Staff Nazarian about raising that back up.

1235
01:39:52,643 --> 01:40:03,825
[SPEAKER_03]: It had been cut to 61, and I asked to go back to the 65 because this is the first election season coming off of re-precincting.

1236
01:40:04,946 --> 01:40:06,266
[SPEAKER_03]: There's a tremendous amount

1237
01:40:07,189 --> 01:40:09,650
[SPEAKER_03]: of work that has to be done.

1238
01:40:10,270 --> 01:40:19,011
[SPEAKER_03]: You have an entire city of 41,000 voters, give or take, that don't know where they're supposed to go vote.

1239
01:40:20,052 --> 01:40:24,933
[SPEAKER_03]: So it's our responsibility to make sure that they know which polling location they're going to.

1240
01:40:25,873 --> 01:40:31,234
[SPEAKER_03]: And then on the splits that the legislature so creatively created for us,

1241
01:40:32,318 --> 01:40:39,420
[SPEAKER_03]: Um, one of them has 66 registered voters, and one of them has 77 registered voters.

1242
01:40:40,441 --> 01:40:45,122
[SPEAKER_03]: That's not enough voters to constitute opening a new polling location.

1243
01:40:45,982 --> 01:40:54,465
[SPEAKER_03]: So what we've been given permission by the state to do is one of them is 6-2-A.

1244
01:40:54,485 --> 01:40:56,946
[SPEAKER_03]: 6-2 is the Brooks School.

1245
01:40:57,886 --> 01:40:59,286
[SPEAKER_03]: So we'll run 6-2-A

1246
01:41:01,436 --> 01:41:10,548
[SPEAKER_03]: with the 77 voters out of that precinct, but I have to have two inspectors and two pullpacks to go with that.

1247
01:41:11,089 --> 01:41:17,318
[SPEAKER_03]: The warden and their ballots will look a little bit different, but they'll still be able to be fed through the same machine.

1248
01:41:19,931 --> 01:41:27,537
[SPEAKER_03]: I've been in contact with LHS as the vendor to create the disks to be able to read those two separate ballots.

1249
01:41:27,998 --> 01:41:30,580
[SPEAKER_03]: I have the same issue in 72 and 72A.

1250
01:41:31,801 --> 01:41:38,486
[SPEAKER_03]: There are 66 active voters in that polling location and we'll do the same thing there.

1251
01:41:39,046 --> 01:41:40,768
[SPEAKER_03]: So that's four additional staff.

1252
01:41:42,509 --> 01:41:46,132
[SPEAKER_03]: Right now, I had one orientation.

1253
01:41:46,352 --> 01:41:49,295
[SPEAKER_03]: I am concerned about having enough staff.

1254
01:41:50,366 --> 01:41:57,651
[SPEAKER_03]: It's, if people are watching the news every day, it's tough everywhere to get election workers.

1255
01:41:58,511 --> 01:42:01,733
[SPEAKER_03]: So the ones that I get and that I have, I want to keep.

1256
01:42:05,275 --> 01:42:11,579
[SPEAKER_03]: That line item is the one that I really would like to see boosted back to where it was.

1257
01:42:12,440 --> 01:42:16,242
[SPEAKER_03]: The other line item that got cut,

1258
