1260
01:42:47,215 --> 01:42:50,616
[SPEAKER_03]: So the office has always been maintained by three full-time people.

1261
01:42:51,196 --> 01:43:04,300
[SPEAKER_03]: And then we've brought in temporary, say 20 to 25 hours a week, four weeks prior to the election to help us process everything that comes in, which is all about scanning.

1262
01:43:04,980 --> 01:43:08,901
[SPEAKER_03]: So it's not something that anybody can key enter, but it's scanning.

1263
01:43:09,561 --> 01:43:11,062
[SPEAKER_03]: And that's a tremendous help to us.

1264
01:43:11,462 --> 01:43:14,383
[SPEAKER_03]: Or they answer the phones because they're ringing off the hooks.

1265
01:43:18,090 --> 01:43:21,092
[SPEAKER_03]: they took out all of the overtime for clerical.

1266
01:43:21,752 --> 01:43:38,241
[SPEAKER_03]: So I asked that $12,000 be put back in that line item to cover the overtime for the two existing positions that are in that office.

1267
01:43:40,643 --> 01:43:44,345
[SPEAKER_03]: And those are the two things that really jumped out at me.

1268
01:43:45,625 --> 01:43:48,946
[SPEAKER_03]: I wanted to be more detailed initially when I did this.

1269
01:43:50,506 --> 01:43:54,907
[SPEAKER_03]: I wanted to be more detailed about exactly what was being spent on what.

1270
01:43:55,928 --> 01:44:06,890
[SPEAKER_03]: And if you go to data processing, the $22,000 that's there, that money is there for the annual street listing.

1271
01:44:08,270 --> 01:44:14,452
[SPEAKER_03]: My hope is that by the time next year comes and the system has all been cleaned up and I can

1272
01:44:15,671 --> 01:44:17,593
