02:00:05,125 --> 02:00:09,690
[SPEAKER_01]: I'll just preface by saying thank you chief of staff Nazarian for your responses and thank you again coordinator girl for being here.

1443
02:00:10,330 --> 02:00:32,885
[SPEAKER_01]: But I appreciate your going just a little bit into the issue of, you know, proper funding for the part time roles to make sure that you have the capacity that you and by you I really mean the city needs to make sure that our upcoming election which will be here really before we know it goes smoothly goes the way that we need it to go securely, you know, leaves everybody feeling secure.

1444
02:00:34,534 --> 02:00:39,795
[SPEAKER_01]: know, the issue of funding is an issue of being able to attract candidates, being able to retain candidates.

1445
02:00:39,855 --> 02:00:46,177
[SPEAKER_01]: I know that that's a concern of yours because you have a vested interest in making sure the election goes well.

1446
02:00:46,277 --> 02:00:46,757
[SPEAKER_01]: That's your job.

1447
02:00:47,537 --> 02:00:59,100
[SPEAKER_01]: Just speaking for myself as a councillor, to echo Vice President Behrs' point, looking at the functioning of the elections office overall, I have the same concerns about

1448
02:01:00,965 --> 02:01:19,233
[SPEAKER_01]: you know, the most top line staff members, you know, that we have to carry out city business, that issue of making sure that we are offering the level of funding to maintain the capacity that we really need to serve our most essential function.

1449
02:01:19,273 --> 02:01:20,793
[SPEAKER_01]: So I just wanted to state that for the record.

1450
02:01:21,274 --> 02:01:25,975
[SPEAKER_01]: You know, as it's been said, I know this is a very, very difficult budget decision, but

1451
02:01:28,319 --> 02:01:30,280
[SPEAKER_01]: These elections are coming up too fast.

1452
02:01:30,580 --> 02:01:40,906
[SPEAKER_01]: These problems, you know, the issue of modernizing our elections department, I would characterize an issue to confront and solve with urgency.

1453
02:01:42,026 --> 02:01:51,932
[SPEAKER_01]: These things are so much on the short-term horizon that it's really hard for me to countenance putting off an essential investment to make sure that these things go the way that they need to.

1454
02:01:52,292 --> 02:01:53,352
[SPEAKER_01]: So thank you for indulging me.

1455
02:01:53,372 --> 02:01:54,513
[SPEAKER_01]: I just wanted to say that for the record.

1456
02:01:55,392 --> 02:01:56,233
[SPEAKER_12]: Thank you, Councillor Collins.

1457
02:01:56,273 --> 02:01:57,654
[SPEAKER_12]: Anything further on elections?

