02:01:57,894 --> 02:02:00,836
[SPEAKER_06]: Mr. President, one last question.

1459
02:02:01,717 --> 02:02:06,580
[SPEAKER_06]: Like we've done in the past, we've put the horse before the cart again.

1460
02:02:07,220 --> 02:02:11,243
[SPEAKER_06]: I mean, we shouldn't be posting a job until this council approves it first.

1461
02:02:12,184 --> 02:02:14,525
[SPEAKER_06]: So again, just a procedural thing.

1462
02:02:15,105 --> 02:02:20,069
[SPEAKER_06]: And that's how we've gotten into some pretty sticky positions in here over the past.

1463
02:02:20,649 --> 02:02:20,869
[SPEAKER_06]: Yeah.

1464
02:02:21,410 --> 02:02:24,472
[SPEAKER_06]: So I would think the prudent practice would be

1465
02:02:25,482 --> 02:02:28,585
[SPEAKER_06]: before you post a job, send it to the council and approve the cap.

1466
02:02:29,245 --> 02:02:33,529
[SPEAKER_06]: What if you go and hire somebody and we don't approve the cap?

1467
02:02:33,549 --> 02:02:37,412
[SPEAKER_12]: Apparently, they just get paid anyway, even though we don't have a full opinion allowing it.

1468
02:02:37,472 --> 02:02:42,977
[SPEAKER_06]: The proper procedure should be coming to us first to approve the position with the cap before you post the job.

1469
02:02:44,718 --> 02:02:45,879
