1512
02:07:39,732 --> 02:07:46,837
[SPEAKER_03]: I was having a little difficulty understanding exactly what I was seeing.

1513
02:07:47,697 --> 02:07:52,641
[SPEAKER_03]: And I went to finance and asked Mr. Lovell for help.

1514
02:07:52,921 --> 02:07:59,506
[SPEAKER_03]: And he came over and looked at what I had and said, no, that's not the budget you are supposed to be looking at.

1515
02:08:00,327 --> 02:08:09,454
[SPEAKER_03]: I then received from Mr. Lovell, the budget that I'm operating off of, which is salaries part-time, FY23 proposed $64,000.

1516
02:08:14,163 --> 02:08:23,109
[SPEAKER_03]: So if I misquoted by 1,000, I'm sorry, but what I have is FY23 proposed $64,000.

1517
02:08:23,529 --> 02:08:37,478
[SPEAKER_03]: And if you look to the column change, FY22 to FY23, it was $61,000 because I needed those election workers.

1518
02:08:37,558 --> 02:08:43,622
[SPEAKER_03]: This budget has never been done in a way that you know exactly what you're getting for your money.

1519
02:08:44,345 --> 02:09:11,515
[SPEAKER_03]: And when I created this budget back in April, I was line iteming everything to detail because I wanted everyone to know, but in no uncertain terms, do I want anyone to misunderstand that I agreed with Chief of Staff Nazarian in regards to one of the positions being cut and what the one that we cut was the lowest position in the office.

1520
02:09:13,077 --> 02:09:15,458
[SPEAKER_03]: So I just wanna put that on the record.

1521
02:09:15,598 --> 02:09:17,019
[SPEAKER_03]: We did exchange emails.

1522
02:09:17,599 --> 02:09:21,522
[SPEAKER_03]: I did email her this morning regarding the concerns I had.

1523
02:09:21,642 --> 02:09:25,524
[SPEAKER_03]: First, it was about that line item.

1524
02:09:25,704 --> 02:09:35,349
[SPEAKER_03]: And then I think my problem was I just had multiple budgets because I didn't see the one that was coming before the council until last night.

1525
02:09:37,870 --> 02:09:39,792
[SPEAKER_03]: So it is different than,

1526
02:09:40,998 --> 02:09:44,780
[SPEAKER_03]: what I had to work with, receiving it last week.

1527
02:09:48,902 --> 02:09:50,543
[SPEAKER_12]: Thank you, Coordinator Gale.

1528
02:09:53,125 --> 02:09:58,388
[SPEAKER_12]: And yeah, I believe we, if I can just find it all here.

1529
02:10:07,057 --> 02:10:10,619
[SPEAKER_12]: Yeah, you know, we received these budgets within the past two to three days as well.

1530
02:10:10,739 --> 02:10:14,542
[SPEAKER_12]: So, um, I know there's been a lot of drafts going around.

1531
02:10:14,562 --> 02:10:21,907
[SPEAKER_12]: I think again, this speaks to the city council's wish that, uh, you know, that a more

1532
02:10:24,218 --> 02:10:34,288
[SPEAKER_12]: It would have been nice to see how the budget was developed and the assumptions that were made to reach the initial proposals and then the proposals after amendments requiring cuts since June 2nd.

1533
02:10:34,928 --> 02:10:39,593
[SPEAKER_12]: I think we've made extensively that case and sent a number of resolutions regarding that to the administration.

1534
02:10:39,633 --> 02:10:44,878
[SPEAKER_12]: So I won't belabor it, but just again, it's another point of confusion in a series of points of confusion.

